# inc-5v5l: does Dispel Evil's +4/+6 deflection bonus (component 0, xval
# TRAP_EVENT, yval EVICTIM(EV_STRIKE)) actually apply on a REAL attack, not
# just get read from code?
#
# THE SCENE. The loaded orc priest of Aiswin (INCURSION_LOAD, set by
# tools/check_dispel_evil.sh) turns on Free Advancement and Infinite Mana
# (Wizard Mode Switches rows 3 and 8 -- src/Tables.cpp's Wizard Options list:
# Cheat Death, Auto-Identify Items, Free Advancement, Infinite Fatigue,
# Always Rest Safely, Ignore Spell Failure, Know All Spells, Infinite Mana),
# so casting the level-5, 16-mana spell is never refused for mana. He rises
# to character level 11 (inc-wn6m: Dispel Evil carries EF_DROUND, so it lasts
# (CL+1)/2 rounds, src/Magic.cpp; at level 1 it ended before the goblin could
# strike; at level 11 it lasts 6). Freeze Monsters is left OFF on purpose. A
# goblin is summoned one square east BEFORE the cast (RIGHT ENTER, adjacent),
# so it is already in reach when the spell starts. It is hostile and, left
# unfrozen, attacks the caster on its own turn. '.' (Wait One Turn) lets it
# act three times, inside the six-round duration.
#
# THE ORACLE is the game's own combat-roll line, already stored in the
# message log because OPT_STORE_ROLLS is on in tools/gates/Options.Dat
# (src/Fight.cpp:9831-9836 prints "Attack: 1d20 (n) ... vs. Def [<breakdown>
# = N][hit/miss]", and the handler's own e.strDef append -- src/Fight.cpp's
# generic breakdown, this spell's own " +N DispEv" -- lands inside that
# bracket). tools/check_dispel_evil.sh pages the whole log ('v', PGUP*100,
# then PGDN) and greps for "DispEv" in an "Attack:" line. The goblin is the
# only creature in the scene that can attack the caster, so any such line is
# unambiguous.

s
w y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN*2 SPACE
DOWN*5 SPACE
ESC
@include dispel-evil-levelup.keys

w
@choose "Learn Any Spell"
"Dispel Evil" ENTER
@dump:learned

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Goblinkin"
@choose "goblin"
RIGHT ENTER
@while "more --" SPACE
w
@choose "Wake Every Creature"
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:goblin-summoned

m
@choose "Dispel Evil"
@dump:after-cast

.
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:after-wait-1
.
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:after-wait-2
.
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:after-wait-3

v
@dump:messages-bottom
PGUP*100
@dump:messages-top
PGDN*1
@dump:messages-mid1
PGDN*1
@dump:messages-mid2
@while "Messages" ESC
@quit
